  "fusion_node_method": {
    "method": "For Berman phases, the crystal-to-crystalline-parent-oxide leg is evaluated within the internally consistent crystal dataset and oxide fusion Gibbs nodes give each parent crystal-to-liquid standard. For Robie and Hemingway phases, each parent liquid standard is converted from the packaged apparent Gibbs energy to formation Gibbs at T by subtracting the JANAF reference-state element G_app values; the stoichiometric sum is then differenced against the printed R&H crystal formation Gibbs energy, which uses the same formation-from-elements-at-T convention.",
    "liquid_standard_source": "Packaged condensate standards evaluated by the gas layer Gibbs helper; FeO and TiO2 use their packaged liquid-parent functions. Alternate condensate tables shift the liquid leg using the same helper.",
    "source": "Berman (1988), Tables 2, 3a/3b, and Table 5 where applicable; Chase (1998), NIST-JANAF Thermochemical Tables, 4th edition; Robie and Hemingway (1995), USGS Bulletin 2131, cited per phase.",
    "interpolation": "Piecewise linear only between listed source nodes; no endpoint extrapolation.",
    "element_reference_source": "Chase (1998), NIST-JANAF Thermochemical Tables, 4th edition, reference-state element tables; printed G_app nodes are included at crystal source temperatures for audit."
  },
